***Formal Parameters***
```c++
void my_function(int formal_parameter);

int main(){

	return 0;
}
...
```
Formal parameters are the **variables** defined in the function prototype

***Actual Parameters***
```c++
...
int main(){
	return 0;
}
void my_function(int actual_parameter){
...
}
```
Actual parameters are the **Variables or expressions** defined in the function definition.

Can use [[Call by reference]] in the parameters to define an [[Output]]
